<title>BELGIUM: TABLE-BELGIAN YR/YR INFLATION 1.89 PCT IN JULY.</title>
<headline>TABLE-BELGIAN YR/YR INFLATION 1.89 PCT IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Belgian Economics Ministry</p>
<p>released the following data on inflation -</p>
<p>    BELGIAN CONSUMER PRICES     July	 June	 July 1996</p>
<p>    Index (base 100=1988)	 125.30     124.30     122.97</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.80	 0.17	 0.65</p>
<p>    Yr/yr change (in pct)	   1.89	 1.74	 1.92</p>
<p>NOTE - consensus forecast for July CPI 1.69 percent.</p>
<p>    Health index *		  122.78     121.67</p>
<p>    Mth/mth change (in pct)	 0.91	 0.18</p>
<p>NOTE - * excludes unhealthy products such as tobacco,</p>
<p>alcohol and petrol, is used for inflation adjustments of rents</p>
<p>and wages.</p>
<p>The ministry said price rises were mainly seen for foreign</p>
<p>travel, fresh fruit and vegetables and holiday homes.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
</text>
